codex
The follow-up frames revealed a second, subtler issue: although the radius animated for longer, it was oversized to roughly twice the necessary cover radius, so the viewport still turned black too early. I’m correcting the endpoint to the exact farthest-corner distance from the period; this keeps the edge moving visibly and linearly until near the end, then reaches guaranteed full coverage.
